From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: patrickjquinn <patrick.jm.quinn@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 17:30:33 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 273/274] ASoC: mediatek: mt6858: Add the MD1 speech path

Calls need the modem's speech PCM (PCM 1, as the stock audio_device.xml
names it) connected to the amplifiers on I2SOUT1 or the codec on ADDA,
and the microphones connected back to it, while a Hostless Speech front
end holds those back ends open without a memory interface.

Add the PCM 1 DAI with its clock gate and interconnects (downlink into
I2SOUT1, ADDA_DL and UL1 for recording the far end; uplink from
ADDA_UL), the Hostless Speech DAI with the stock routes, and the
machine's front-end and back-end links. The platform pointer callback
returns 0 for the hostless front end, which has no memif to read.

On the Jolla the routes power up (DAPM), PCM 1 enables and the modem
acks speech on. The modem did not clock PCM 1 at 48 kHz (TX FIFO
overflow); far-end audio has not been heard yet.
